## Claude Desktop configuration

Add the deployed Worker URL to `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`:

```jsonc
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "{{ spec_slug }}": {
      "transport": "http",
      "url": "https://{tenant_short_id}-{{ spec_slug }}.mcpgen.dev",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer ${MCPGEN_TENANT_KEY}"{% if auth_mode == "passthrough" %},
        "X-Upstream-Auth": "Bearer ${UPSTREAM_API_KEY}"{% endif %}
      }
    }
  }
}
```

> **Server-name template:** `{tenant_short_id}-{{ spec_slug }}`. Phase 6 deploy
> substitutes `{tenant_short_id}` per tenant — two tenants on the same spec
> never collide (Pitfall #30 mitigation per CONTEXT D-25).

## Authentication

{% if auth_mode == "passthrough" %}
This server uses **pass-through authentication.** Your MCP client must send
the upstream API credential in the `X-Upstream-Auth` header on every request.
The server does NOT persist your credential.
{% elif auth_mode == "stored" %}
This server uses **stored credentials** with AES-256-GCM encryption + a
per-tenant DEK in Cloudflare KV. Provision your upstream credential via
`wrangler secret put UPSTREAM_API_KEY` after deploy.
{% elif auth_mode == "oauth" %}
This server uses **OAuth 2.1** with PKCE through Logto. Configure the OAuth
client at deploy time; visit `/auth/login` from the deployed URL to start
the flow.
{% endif %}

## Regenerating

When the upstream spec changes, regenerate locally:

```bash
mcpgen init {{ spec_url }} --auth-mode {{ auth_mode }}
```

The Phase 8 Drift Watcher monitors `{{ spec_url }}` and surfaces drift in
your dashboard.
